--TEST--
`Core\Mail\Attachment::src` names an image of one message only: a `cid:` of another message's attachment, in any attribute, case or spacing, throws a `RuntimeError` before anything is sent, and `src()` of an attachment that is not inline throws
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Mail\Attachment::src, Core\Mail\Attachment::inlineBytes
use Core\Mail\Attachment;

Attachment $logo = Attachment::inlineBytes('logo.png', 'pixel', { type: 'image/png' });
Attachment $banner = Attachment::inlineBytes('banner.png', 'pixel', { type: 'image/png' });

// The first message uses its own image.
Core\Mail::preview(html`<img src="{$logo->src()}">`, { attachments: [$logo] });
echo "own image: built\n";

// Another message uses the logo's URL without the logo.
try {
    Core\Mail::preview(html`<img src="{$logo->src()}">`);
    echo "no attachment: built\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo "no attachment: ", Core\Str::contains($e->message, $logo->src()) ? 'names the cid' : $e->message, "\n";
}

// Another message attaches its own image and uses the logo's URL.
try {
    Core\Mail::preview(html`<img src="{$logo->src()}">`, { attachments: [$banner] });
    echo "other attachment: built\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e2) {
    echo "other attachment: RuntimeError\n";
}

// Capital letters, a leading space, CSS and a link are each read as a use of the URL.
string $id = Core\Str::slice($logo->src(), 4);
array<Core\Html\Markup> $bodies = [
    html`<img src="CID:{$id}">`,
    html`<img src=" cid:{$id}">`,
    html`<div style="background: url(cid:{$id})">x</div>`,
    html`<a href="cid:{$id}">x</a>`,
];
foreach ($bodies as Core\Html\Markup $body) {
    try {
        Core\Mail::preview($body, { attachments: [$banner] });
        echo "variant: built\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $e3) {
        echo "variant: RuntimeError\n";
    }
}

// A file to download has no `src()`.
try {
    echo Attachment::fromBytes('a.pdf', '%PDF-1.4')->src(), "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e4) {
    echo $e4->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
own image: built
no attachment: names the cid
other attachment: RuntimeError
variant: RuntimeError
variant: RuntimeError
variant: RuntimeError
variant: RuntimeError
Core\Mail\Attachment::src: this attachment is not inline, so it has no `src()`. Build it with `inlineFile` or `inlineBytes` to show it inside the HTML.
